# v1.0.54 (§1.6.50) PART 5 — default Excluded Apps seed list
# v1.0.56 — D1 EXTRACTED: the package names below were read off the operator's
#   device on 2026-10-24 (BLOCK v1.0.56, PART B) and confirmed by the operator
#   with "CONFIRM D1: ALL CLASSIFIED-IRANIAN".
#
# Format, one package name per line:
#
#   com.example.app            ← seeded on first run, IF it is installed
#   # anything after '#' is a comment
#
# Rules the loader enforces (see DefaultExcludedApps.parse):
#   * blank lines and '#' comments are ignored;
#   * a line is cut at the first '#', so a trailing comment on an entry works;
#   * a line is used verbatim as an Android package name — no spaces, no
#     commas, no aliases;
#   * a package that is not installed on the device is SKIPPED, never
#     inserted as a phantom row;
#   * duplicates collapse to the first occurrence;
#   * the seed runs at most ONCE per install (see SETTING_EXCLUDED_APPS_SEEDED),
#     so a user who later removes a seeded app does not get it back.
#
# ── PROVENANCE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Source: the `excluded_apps` table of the on-device database
# `vpn_gate_connector` (device 5585fecc, Xiaomi 2201117TG, Android 13),
# read read-only via `run-as`. Every package below was INSTALLED on that
# device at extraction time (`pm path` returned an APK path for each).
#
# The operator's device carried 15 excluded apps. Three were deliberately NOT
# shipped, because this list is a default for ALL users and not a copy of one
# operator's phone:
#
#   * com.deepseek.chat (DeepSeek) — a Chinese AI assistant, a personal
#     install. Not Iranian; shipping it would silently exclude it inside
#     every user's tunnel.
#   * com.google.android.projection.gearhead (Android Auto) — a Google system
#     app. §1.6.47 records it as the operator's own user-added exclusion, so
#     it belongs to that device's data, not to the shipped default.
#   * vn.unlimit.vpngatepro (Self) — the app excludes itself automatically in
#     `App.kt`; listing it here would be a duplicate.
#
# The 12 entries below are the ones classified "clearly Iranian" and confirmed
# by the operator. They are sorted alphabetically by package name.
#
# ── WHY THE ENTRIES ARE HERE AT ALL ───────────────────────────────────────
#
# The seed exists so that a fresh install already excludes the Iranian
# services the operator uses, instead of asking them to tick a dozen boxes by
# hand. The names are data, not code: adding, removing or re-annotating an
# entry is an edit to this one file — no code change, no schema change, no
# migration — because the parsing, the installed check, the one-shot flag and
# the tests are already done.

